{"availability":"available","full":"abhid1234/time-to-index","name":"time-to-index","description":"How long does a newly published fact take to reach a web-search API - and does the API say ABSENT, or confidently serve the superseded answer?","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-31T02:14:00Z","updated":"2026-10-17T04:41:04Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://abhid1234.github.io/time-to-index/","topics":["benchmark","freshness","information-retrieval","llm-agents","rag","staleness","survival-analysis","web-search"],"demo":"https://abhid1234.github.io/time-to-index/playground.html","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T05:14:16.060Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T05:14:16.060Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T05:14:16.060Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T06:14:20.045Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T05:14:16.060Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Time to Index measures how long a newly published fact takes to become retrievable through a web-search API — and, until it does, what the API returns instead. It separates two failures that other search benchmarks score the same way: returning nothing (ABSENT) and confidently returning the answer that was just replaced (STALE). It does not crawl, does not rank providers it cannot separate statistically, and does not trust anyone's clock but the publisher's."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/abhid1234/time-to-index/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9392fb13b943e848e7142653a0a59b1a214a615f7dd4daf45b92ef15827c8217","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:52.229Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:20.181Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Time to Index measures how long a newly published fact takes to become retrievable through a web-search API — and, until it does, what the API returns instead. It separates two failures that other se